C03: a go-to order cut on a preposition is a cut request even when short (UI1641)

«Ve a Cotele en» stops on a bare preposition after a go-to head; the cut-request reader (FILES H0426) needed six words, so the mind read the four-word order as a web navigation to the name before the cut. Under a go-to head («ve a», «andá a», «entrá a», «go to», «llevame a») four words now suffice: the turn quotes the cut tail and asks how the message continues, and navigates nowhere.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


